# Frontend starter

This directory is a placeholder for the browser app that will connect to the FastAPI backend.

A practical option is a Vite React app or Next.js app hosted on Firebase Hosting.

## Recommended flow

```bash
npm create vite@latest antigravity-frontend -- --template react
cd antigravity-frontend
npm install
```

Then connect the frontend to the backend at `http://localhost:8080` during local development.

## Minimal flow

- Use WebSocket to `/ws/chat/{session_id}`
- Use fetch or Axios to `/chat/start`
- Render streaming text and tool updates
- Add model selector and login flow

## Production

For production, deploy the frontend to Firebase Hosting and the backend to Cloud Run.

## Notes

The key logic is already defined by the Mobile Harness project: it uses Antigravity stream JSON events and tool parsing. Reuse that pattern in the browser frontend.
